ual-area-program"},"revisionId":"sha256:45074cc4cd63fa946718dfc5c0d99ff79140490dd900317cb8dfdd85b7003c12","revisionNumber":1,"status":"active","subjects":[],"summary":"This program studies the geometric and affine consequences of taking D, E, and F as the side midpoints of a nondegenerate triangle ABC. Established knowledge includes the midpoint-segment relations, quarter-area results for the medial and corner triangles, half-scaling of the relevant corner altitudes, and equality of all four small areas. Formal verification remains prospective, and there is no supplied active mathematical dispute.","title":"Triangle-midpoint area structure"}
{"action":"create","baseRevisionId":null,"changeRationale":"This lemma is materialized as a distinct durable concept because the vector identities independently establish the midpoint-segment geometry used by several area arguments. The cited judgment specifically distinguishes this derivation from the transaction event that supplied it.","changeRef":{"artifact":"report.md","digest":"sha256:e967a536546649d8e8c990aea26769420f6c85ec79a6df718972ff79f5fc455e","section":"## Change: triangle-midpoints/midpoint-segment-relations"},"contentDigest":"sha256:d612892ebefe4226e7e81ae667a86776f2917531144c75f31866c26238e69198","evidence":[{"digest":"sha256:575cfe733758035c57b6a7f7915c3e2a38a78c25f4b0c6ce026504546e4655ed","id":"sha256:575cfe733758035c57b6a7f7915c3e2a38a78c25f4b0c6ce026504546e4655ed","kind":"judgment","relation":"supports"},{"digest":"sha256:427537f9898af49bb7e20230201f0ab01db5a51cccbfdb5b57c474e488b3a262","id":"sha256:427537f9898af49bb7e20230201f0ab01db5a51cccbfdb5b57c474e488b3a262","kind":"judgment","relation":"supports"},{"digest":null,"id":"4ccbe3f18db7402d31a2ef795f6ad67962ff63e3","kind":"transaction","relation":"supports"},{"digest":null,"id":"64afc12868e150370e6c56e6eeceab6b7aabe158","kind":"transaction","relation":"supports"}],"facets":["topology","content","lifecycle","provenance"],"nodeId":"triangle-midpoints/midpoint-segment-relations","nodeType":"lemma","parentId":"triangle-midpoints/equal-area-program","recordedAtLedgerHead":"a7acd1ec3554f51b381784ff2f84663b88e9c262","reportRef":{"artifact":"report.md","digest":"sha256:e967a536546649d8e8c990aea26769420f6c85ec79a6df718972ff79f5fc455e","section":"## Node: triangle-midpoints/midpoint-segment-relations"},"revisionId":"sha256:ce1ffed76e1f9f162e839db7d7ef788bada338b87dea2e895a1f03787b0f3468","revisionNumber":1,"status":"active","subjects":[{"id":"4ccbe3f18db7402d31a2ef795f6ad67962ff63e3","kind":"transaction","ledgerPosition":2}],"summary":"For D=(B+C)/2, E=(C+A)/2, and F=(A+B)/2, the accepted vector identities show EF is parallel to BC, FD is parallel to CA, and DE is parallel to AB, with each midpoint segment having half the length of its corresponding side. Endpoint-order signs do not affect these parallelism or length conclusions.","title":"Parallelism and half-length relations for triangle midpoint segments"}
{"action":"create","baseRevisionId":null,"changeRationale":"This result is created separately from the midpoint-segment lemma because it records the durable area consequence of the accepted half-scale similarity, rather than the underlying segment relations themselves.","changeRef":{"artifact":"report.md","digest":"sha256:e967a536546649d8e8c990aea26769420f6c85ec79a6df718972ff79f5fc455e","section":"## Change: triangle-midpoints/medial-triangle-quarter-area"},"contentDigest":"sha256:c4d804f7820f3e254ee4d908b46084fb97f31e708d2933a37f608d52ca6f60cd","evidence":[{"digest":"sha256:427537f9898af49bb7e20230201f0ab01db5a51cccbfdb5b57c474e488b3a262","id":"sha256:427537f9898af49bb7e20230201f0ab01db5a51cccbfdb5b57c474e488b3a262","kind":"judgment","relation":"supports"},{"digest":"sha256:575cfe733758035c57b6a7f7915c3e2a38a78c25f4b0c6ce026504546e4655ed","id":"sha256:575cfe733758035c57b6a7f7915c3e2a38a78c25f4b0c6ce026504546e4655ed","kind":"judgment","relation":"supports"},{"digest":null,"id":"64afc12868e150370e6c56e6eeceab6b7aabe158","kind":"transaction","relation":"supports"},{"digest":null,"id":"4ccbe3f18db7402d31a2ef795f6ad67962ff63e3","kind":"transaction","relation":"supports"}],"facets":["topology","content","lifecycle","provenance"],"nodeId":"triangle-midpoints/medial-triangle-quarter-area","nodeType":"result","parentId":"triangle-midpoints/equal-area-program","recordedAtLedgerHead":"a7acd1ec3554f51b381784ff2f84663b88e9c262","reportRef":{"artifact":"report.md","digest":"sha256:e967a536546649d8e8c990aea26769420f6c85ec79a6df718972ff79f5fc455e","section":"## Node: triangle-midpoints/medial-triangle-quarter-area"},"revisionId":"sha256:e822bfe0e171d102cb3dc93743f8410392318850199f723ad2ed26eb47b3f5c0","revisionNumber":1,"status":"active","subjects":[],"summary":"The midpoint-segment half-length relations make DEF similar to ABC with linear scale factor 1/2. The accepted area-scaling law for similar triangles therefore gives [DEF]=[ABC]/4. The ordinary midpoint-theorem proof is complete; the vector derivation explicitly supplies the same supporting relations.","title":"Area of the medial triangle"}
{"action":"create","baseRevisionId":null,"changeRationale":"This result is created as the stable home for the accepted quarter-area conclusions for all three corner triangles. It consolidates the included-angle, similarity, homothety, and corrected base-height routes without treating any contributing transaction as a knowledge node.","changeRef":{"artifact":"report.md","digest":"sha256:e967a536546649d8e8c990aea26769420f6c85ec79a6df718972ff79f5fc455e","section":"## Change: triangle-midpoints/corner-triangles-quarter-area"},"contentDigest":"sha256:9a5305dc1356b612322773d46e13e9c6deb92d70da2904255fc687cfed80fcdf","evidence":[{"digest":"sha256:427537f9898af49bb7e20230201f0ab01db5a51cccbfdb5b57c474e488b3a262","id":"sha256:427537f9898af49bb7e20230201f0ab01db5a51cccbfdb5b57c474e488b3a262","kind":"judgment","relation":"supports"},{"digest":"sha256:575cfe733758035c57b6a7f7915c3e2a38a78c25f4b0c6ce026504546e4655ed","id":"sha256:575cfe733758035c57b6a7f7915c3e2a38a78c25f4b0c6ce026504546e4655ed","kind":"judgment","relation":"supports"},{"digest":"sha256:ae48d86e7bd2cdc4b6c2a708194553c6c8444c7f448bd73a82f8af95b64580c3","id":"sha256:ae48d86e7bd2cdc4b6c2a708194553c6c8444c7f448bd73a82f8af95b64580c3","kind":"judgment","relation":"supports"},{"digest":null,"id":"64afc12868e150370e6c56e6eeceab6b7aabe158","kind":"transaction","relation":"supports"},{"digest":null,"id":"4ccbe3f18db7402d31a2ef795f6ad67962ff63e3","kind":"transaction","relation":"supports"},{"digest":null,"id":"8bcf66bbd7777ee31f637a0a1a144535feb82ba4","kind":"transaction","relation":"supports"}],"facets":["topology","content","lifecycle","provenance"],"nodeId":"triangle-midpoints/corner-triangles-quarter-area","nodeType":"result","parentId":"triangle-midpoints/equal-area-program","recordedAtLedgerHead":"a7acd1ec3554f51b381784ff2f84663b88e9c262","reportRef":{"artifact":"report.md","digest":"sha256:e967a536546649d8e8c990aea26769420f6c85ec79a6df718972ff79f5fc455e","section":"## Node: triangle-midpoints/corner-triangles-quarter-area"},"revisionId":"sha256:d1867460b11d20bc767a411edcd53b3598431e9e25a153388d1af8127a586386","revisionNumber":1,"status":"active","subjects":[],"summary":"The judgments establish [AEF]=[BFD]=[CDE]=[ABC]/4. Accepted justifications include the included-angle area formula, half-scale similarity, vertex-centered homothety, and a base-height calculation in which both the midpoint base and corresponding altitude scale by 1/2. Under nondegeneracy, the three areas are positive.","title":"Areas of the three corner midpoint triangles"}
{"action":"create","baseRevisionId":null,"changeRationale":"This node is created beneath the corner-area result because the judged altitude ratio is a reusable geometric lemma and a necessary constraint on the base-height method. It also preserves the judgment’s attribution limitation without creating an unsupported conflict or report-shaped node.","changeRef":{"artifact":"report.md","digest":"sha256:e967a536546649d8e8c990aea26769420f6c85ec79a6df718972ff79f5fc455e","section":"## Change: triangle-midpoints/corner-altitude-scaling"},"contentDigest":"sha256:a1dc7d7d399aa513dd9f9de3e0711afc2b5dc9556ffa4e660dec325e61e80840","evidence":[{"digest":"sha256:ae48d86e7bd2cdc4b6c2a708194553c6c8444c7f448bd73a82f8af95b64580c3","id":"sha256:ae48d86e7bd2cdc4b6c2a708194553c6c8444c7f448bd73a82f8af95b64580c3","kind":"judgment","relation":"supports"},{"digest":null,"id":"8bcf66bbd7777ee31f637a0a1a144535feb82ba4","kind":"transaction","relation":"supports"},{"digest":null,"id":"64afc12868e150370e6c56e6eeceab6b7aabe158","kind":"transaction","relation":"context"},{"digest":null,"id":"4ccbe3f18db7402d31a2ef795f6ad67962ff63e3","kind":"transaction","relation":"context"}],"facets":["topology","content","lifecycle","provenance"],"nodeId":"triangle-midpoints/corner-altitude-scaling","nodeType":"lemma","parentId":"triangle-midpoints/corner-triangles-quarter-area","recordedAtLedgerHead":"a7acd1ec3554f51b381784ff2f84663b88e9c262","reportRef":{"artifact":"report.md","digest":"sha256:e967a536546649d8e8c990aea26769420f6c85ec79a6df718972ff79f5fc455e","section":"## Node: triangle-midpoints/corner-altitude-scaling"},"revisionId":"sha256:5344507a0d9082758b4b51267eb0065259a124e6f467759e9d8495bc04ad86bc","revisionNumber":1,"status":"active","subjects":[{"id":"8bcf66bbd7777ee31f637a0a1a144535feb82ba4","kind":"transaction","ledgerPosition":3}],"summary":"Under the factor-1/2 homothety centered at a corner, the opposite side maps to the corresponding midpoint segment and point-to-line distances scale by 1/2. Thus the altitude to the midpoint segment is half, not equal to, the altitude to the original opposite side; cyclic analogues hold at the other vertices. The unsupplied source of the rejected wording limits attribution but not the accepted mathematical conclusion.","title":"Altitude scaling under the corner midpoint homothety"}
